feat(hybrid): match QEMU fast-leg ISA to the vsim engine via -readconfig

A hybrid run now configures the QEMU producer leg with the selected
accurate engine's full ISA, not a fixed -cpu string. run_plan probes the
engine's `--print-qemu-config` (a QEMU -readconfig cfg distilled from its
config.inc), stages it under the plan workdir, and plan_argvs injects
`-readconfig <cfg>` into the fast (QEMU) leg only.

Tolerant: an engine without the flag (its parser throws on the unknown
option -> non-zero exit) leaves the cfg empty and the fast leg keeps its
default -cpu -- no regression. The vsim accurate leg never sees -readconfig.

The producer side (vsim --print-qemu-config + the build-time bake from
config.inc, via the cpu_config_to_march_converter submodule) lives in the
hybrid_vsim repo. See docs/qemu_match_ROADMAP.md.

- FA1: plan_argvs fast-leg -readconfig injection (plan_test.cpp)
- FA2: stage_qemu_cfg probe + tolerant fallback (plan_test.cpp)
- docs: USER_GUIDE hw-config sync, engine_interface optional capability,
  qemu_match_ROADMAP, print-qemu-config smoke test

Behavioral change.

